      "passage": "<p>In 1985, a riot at a Brussels soccer match occurred, in which many fans lost their lives. The __(16)__ began 45 minutes before the start of the European Cup final. The British team was scheduled to __(17)__ the Italian team in the game. Noisy British fans, after setting off some rockets and fireworks to cheer for __(18)__ team, broke through a thin wire fence and started to attack the Italian fans. The Italians, in panic, __(19)__ the main exit in their section when a six-foot concrete wall collapsed. By the end of the night, 38 soccer fans had died and 437 were injured. The majority of the deaths resulted from people __(20)__ trampled underfoot or crushed against barriers in the stadium. As a result of this 1985 soccer incident, security measures have since been tightened at major sports competitions to prevent similar events from happening.</p>"
